<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Webspresso Client Behavior Layer — Live Demo</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/demo.css">
</head>
<body>
  <nav class="demo-nav">
    <a class="demo-nav-brand" href="/">⚡ Webspresso Client Behavior</a>
    <div class="demo-nav-links">
      <a href="/todos">1. Todo List (Full Showcase)</a>
      <a href="/counter">2. SSR Counter (Zero .client.*)</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <h1>Webspresso Client Behavior Layer (<code>core/client</code>)</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Explore the two interactive SSR + Datastar examples below:</p>

    <div class="demo-card">
      <h2>1. Todo List — Filtered &amp; Paginated Tasks + Draft Preservation + Explicit API</h2>
      <p>
        Features live KPI progress bar (<code>todos-summary</code> fragment), filtered &amp; paginated task list
        (<code>todos-list</code> fragment), single-click task completion/deletion, bulk actions, server-side Zod validation
        with accessible error focus, an open Edit Draft card that preserves unsaved input during refreshes, and an explicit
        <code>api.get('/api/todos/insights')</code> client state panel.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/todos" style="color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600;">Open Todo List Showcase →</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="demo-card">
      <h2>2. Server-Fragment Counter (Zero <code>.client.*</code> File)</h2>
      <p>
        Renders the counter via an SSR fragment (<code>{{ "{{ fsy.fragment('count') }}" }}</code>) and updates it via a native
        <code>&lt;form action="/api/counter" method="post" data-w-form="counter-increment"&gt;</code>.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/counter" style="color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600;">Open Counter Demo →</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
